  "rationale": "**Structural check passes. I did not assess behavior or tests.**\n\n- **`SourceAnalysis::parse` signature.** The `parse` method is in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[parse]`. It is declared `pub async fn parse(&self, id: &ResourceId) -> Result<ParsedSource, P::Error>`. That is exactly the required signature. It sits in `impl<P: SourceProvider> SourceAnalysis<P>`, which matches the bound in the requirement. Its body delegates to `self.provider.parse(id, &self.languages)`, so it goes through the `SourceProvider` interface. `SourceAnalysis<P>` is a public struct with public `provider` and `languages` fields.\n- **`SourceTools` exposes `read_source`.** `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<'_, P, F, D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` declares a `read_source` tool. Its parameters are a required `resource` and an optional `selector`. The sibling `fn[dispatch]` handles the `\"read_source\"` name. It deserializes the resource, resolves the selector and records the observation.\n\nI found no missing or conflicting structural element. There are no acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
